<div class="ap-report ap-outbound" data-outbound-reports>
  <header class="ap-report-header"><div><span class="ap-report-brand">Atlas <span>/ OUTBOUND INTELLIGENCE</span></span><h4>See what leaves your network.</h4><p>Reports modeled from an anonymized outbound sample</p></div><span class="ap-sample-label"><i aria-hidden="true"></i> Selected files</span></header>
  <div class="ap-report-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Outbound reports" hidden>
    <button type="button" role="tab" id="report-tab-activity" aria-controls="report-activity" aria-selected="true"><span>01</span> Shipping activity</button>
    <button type="button" role="tab" id="report-tab-trace" aria-controls="report-trace" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><span>02</span> Lot traceability</button>
    <button type="button" role="tab" id="report-tab-shelf" aria-controls="report-shelf" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><span>03</span> Shelf life</button>
  </div>
  <section id="report-activity" class="ap-report-panel">
    <h5 class="ap-report-fallback">Shipping activity</h5>
    <div class="ap-report-metrics"><div><span>Shipping events</span><strong>{{ atlasOutbound.shippingLabel }}</strong><small>Distinct event IDs in the sample</small></div><div><span>Outbound partners</span><strong>{{ atlasOutbound.partners }}</strong><small>Represented in the selected files</small></div><div><span>Product lots traced</span><strong>{{ atlasOutbound.lots }}</strong><small>Connected through serialized items</small></div></div>
    <div class="ap-report-body">
      <figure class="ap-shipping-chart"><figcaption><div><strong>Shipping activity, in context.</strong><span>Selected files · May–October 2026</span></div><span class="ap-chart-unit">Shipping events</span></figcaption>
        <div class="ap-shipping-bars" aria-label="Shipping events by month">
          {% for month in atlasOutbound.months %}<button type="button" class="ap-shipping-bar" data-shipping-month="{{ month.longLabel }}" data-shipping-count="{{ month.value }}" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if loop.last else 'false' }}" aria-label="{{ month.longLabel }}: {{ month.value }} shipping events"><span class="ap-shipping-bar-plot"><span class="ap-shipping-bar-fill" style="height:{{ month.height }}%"><b>{{ month.value }}</b></span></span><span class="ap-shipping-bar-label">{{ month.label }}</span></button>{% endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="ap-chart-selection" aria-live="polite"><strong data-selected-month>October 2026</strong><span><b data-selected-count>183</b> shipping events in the selected files.</span></p>
      </figure>
      <aside class="ap-report-insight"><span class="ap-insight-kicker">ATLAS OBSERVATION</span><h5>Event volume is not shipment volume.</h5><p>The files contain <strong>{{ atlasOutbound.eventsLabel }} events</strong>, but only <strong>{{ atlasOutbound.shippingLabel }}</strong> describe shipping. Commissioning and packing records supply the history behind them.</p><button type="button" class="ap-report-link" data-open-report="trace" hidden>Explore the traceability →</button></aside>
    </div>
    <p class="ap-report-scope">The timeline covers 2,250 selected shipping events from May–October 2026. October is partial.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="report-trace" class="ap-report-panel">
    <h5 class="ap-report-fallback">Lot traceability</h5>
    <div class="ap-report-metrics"><div><span>Serialized items traced</span><strong class="ap-metric-long">{{ atlasOutbound.serialsLabel }}</strong><small>Distinct item identifiers</small></div><div><span>Product lots connected</span><strong>{{ atlasOutbound.lots }}</strong><small>Product and lot combinations</small></div><div><span>Shipping events mapped</span><strong>{{ atlasOutbound.shippingLabel }}</strong><small>Packaging linked to commissioning</small></div></div>
    <div class="ap-trace-body">
      <div class="ap-trace-heading"><div><h5>Follow the record back to the lot.</h5><p>Three anonymized examples from the selected files.</p></div><div class="ap-range" role="group" aria-label="Traceability example">{% for example in atlasOutbound.examples %}<button type="button" data-trace-example="{{ loop.index0 }}" data-containers="{{ example.containers }}" data-items="{{ example.items }}" data-lots="{{ example.lots }}" data-days="{{ example.days }}" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if loop.first else 'false' }}">{{ example.label }}</button>{% endfor %}</div></div>
      <div class="ap-trace-chain" aria-live="polite"><div><span class="ap-trace-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span>Outbound record</span><strong>1</strong><small>Shipping event</small></div><span class="ap-trace-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span class="ap-trace-symbol" aria-hidden="true">▦</span><span>Packaging hierarchy</span><strong data-trace-value="containers">{{ atlasOutbound.examples[0].containers }}</strong><small>Connected containers</small></div><span class="ap-trace-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span class="ap-trace-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⋮⋮</span><span>Serialized items</span><strong data-trace-value="items">{{ atlasOutbound.examples[0].items }}</strong><small>Traced through the hierarchy</small></div><span class="ap-trace-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="ap-trace-lot"><span class="ap-trace-symbol" aria-hidden="true">◈</span><span>Product lots</span><strong data-trace-value="lots">{{ atlasOutbound.examples[0].lots }}</strong><small>With lot and expiration dates</small></div></div>
      <div class="ap-trace-finding"><div><span class="ap-insight-kicker">FOLLOW THE QUESTION</span><p>The shortest remaining shelf life in <span data-trace-label>Example 01</span> is <strong><span data-trace-value="days">{{ atlasOutbound.examples[0].days }}</span> days</strong>. The packaging links let the team connect that date to the shipped items.</p></div><button type="button" class="ap-report-link" data-open-report="shelf" hidden>Look at shelf life →</button></div>
      <figure class="ap-history-mix"><figcaption><strong>The history behind the shipping records</strong><span>All {{ atlasOutbound.eventsLabel }} event entries in the sample</span></figcaption><div class="ap-history-stack" aria-hidden="true">{% for step in atlasOutbound.steps %}<i style="width:{{ step.share }}%" class="ap-history-segment--{{ loop.index0 }}"></i>{% endfor %}</div><ul>{% for step in atlasOutbound.steps %}<li><i class="ap-history-segment--{{ loop.index0 }}" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>{{ step.label }}</span><strong>{{ step.formatted }}</strong></li>{% endfor %}</ul></figure>
    </div>
    <p class="ap-report-scope">Counts come from three selected shipping events. Identifying details are withheld.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="report-shelf" class="ap-report-panel">
    <h5 class="ap-report-fallback">Shelf life at shipment</h5>
    <div class="ap-shelf-controls"><div><h5>How much shelf life leaves with each shipment?</h5><p>Compare the recorded expiration date with the shipping date.</p></div><div><span class="ap-control-label">Illustrative review window</span><div class="ap-range" role="group" aria-label="Shelf-life review window"><button type="button" data-shelf-window="90" aria-pressed="false">90 days</button><button type="button" data-shelf-window="180" aria-pressed="false">180 days</button><button type="button" data-shelf-window="365" aria-pressed="true">365 days</button></div></div></div>
    <div class="ap-report-metrics"><div><span>Lot checks</span><strong>{{ atlasOutbound.lotChecksLabel }}</strong><small>One lot per shipping event</small></div><div><span>Within the review window</span><strong data-shelf-count>{{ atlasOutbound.review365 }}</strong><small data-shelf-window-label>365 days or less remaining</small></div><div><span>Shipping events with lot dates</span><strong>{{ atlasOutbound.datedShippingLabel }}</strong><small>{{ atlasOutbound.missingDates }} could not be assessed for shelf life</small></div></div>
    <div class="ap-report-body">
      <figure class="ap-shelf-chart"><figcaption><strong>Remaining shelf life at shipment</strong><span>Count of lot checks · bar lengths show share of checks</span></figcaption><div class="ap-shelf-rows">{% for bucket in atlasOutbound.shelfBuckets %}<div class="ap-shelf-row{{ ' is-review' if bucket.limit <= 365 else '' }}" data-shelf-bucket data-limit="{{ bucket.limit }}" data-count="{{ bucket.value }}"><span>{{ bucket.label }}</span><i><b style="width:{{ bucket.share }}%"></b></i><strong>{{ bucket.formatted }}</strong></div>{% endfor %}</div></figure>
      <aside class="ap-report-insight"><span class="ap-insight-kicker">ATLAS OBSERVATION</span><h5 data-shelf-headline>Focus the review on 62 lot checks.</h5><p data-shelf-observation>62 of 12,603 lot checks fall within the selected 365-day window. Compare them with your agreed requirements before deciding on a next step.</p><a class="ap-report-link" href="#atlas-systems" data-atlas-step>Connect the context →</a></aside>
    </div>
    <p class="ap-report-scope">Each lot is counted once per shipping event. Separate shipments count separately. Set the review window around your business requirements.</p>
  </section>
  <details class="ap-report-method"><summary>About these report models</summary><div><p>Built from {{ atlasOutbound.files }} selected outbound EPCIS files. Counts are computed from the sample; customer names, identifiers and source files are withheld. The sample does not represent the complete outbound history. Nine older shipping events are outside the timeline shown.</p><p>Shipping activity uses distinct shipping-event IDs. Traceability follows the included packing relationships to commissioning records. Shelf life uses the recorded shipping and expiration dates for each linked product lot. {{ atlasOutbound.missingDates }} shipping events lack assessable lot-date context in this sample.</p><p>These outbound records describe shipping and its supporting history. Receipt and current inventory would require additional data. Review windows and system connections would be designed with your team.</p></div></details>
</div>
